    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Farrell Auctioneers Valuers & Estate Agents Ltd. are delighted to bring to the market this detached four-bedroom, two-storey residence, situated in the peaceful rural setting of Roxton, Corofin, Co. Clare.\n\nBuilt in 1993, the property offers spacious and versatile accommodation comprising a kitchen/living/dining area, four bedrooms, and a family bathroom. The property requires renovation and modernisation, presenting an excellent opportunity for a purchaser to create a home to their own taste and requirements.The property is approached via an electric gated entrance, with a private laneway winding through mature hazel woodland and leading to a further security gate. A generous gravelled parking area provides space for approximately four to five cars, while the surrounding grounds offer excellent potential for landscaping and outdoor enjoyment.\n\nLocated close to Corofin village, the property is within easy reach of local shops, schools, sporting facilities, and other amenities. Ennis is also within comfortable commuting distance, offering a wider range of services and facilities.\n\nThis property presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a private countryside home with significant potential for renovation and modernisation, in an attractive and tranquil location in County Clare.\n\nPlease contact our office on 091 - 632688 or email colm@colmfarrell.com to arrange to view the property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Sitting Room - 3.85m (12'8\") x 2.6m (8'6\")\nThis room has carpet flooring. Hand built stone fireplace with Liscannor stone mantle and hearth. Solid fuel stove. Double aspect windows. SE and SW facing\n\nKitchen - 3.8m (12'6\") x 2.65m (8'8\")\nThis area has a tiled floor. Fitted counter top and shelving units. SS sink with micra tap and drinking tap. It also has an oil range and a gas cooker. Double aspect windows. SE and NE facing windows.\n\nDining room - 3.6m (11'10\") x 2.8m (9'2\")\nThis room has carpet flooring. Sliding patio door to garden. Double acces to sitting room and kitchen.\n\nUnderstairs Storage area - 2m (6'7\") x 0.8m (2'7\")\nThis area has a tiled floor.\n\nEntrance Reception - 2.8m (9'2\") x 1.85m (6'1\")\nThis area has a tled floor. NW facing front door and window. Hotpress with shelving. Wooden staircase with carpet to first floor\n\nBathroom - 2.6m (8'6\") x 2.5m (8'2\")\nThis room has vilyn flooring. A bath with shower overhead. Shower area is tiled floor to ceiling. New electric micra elite shower. WC and WHB.\n\nDownstairs bedroom - 2.65m (8'8\") x 2.5m (8'2\")\nThis room has carpet flooring. SW facing window\n\nUpstairs landing area - 2.9m (9'6\") x 0.9m (2'11\")\nThis area has a carpet flooring. A vaulted ceiling with exposed beams.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.9m (12'10\") x 2.6m (8'6\")\nThis area has carpet flooring. Vaulted ceiling with exposed wooden beams. NE facing windows.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.6m (8'6\") x 2.3m (7'7\")\nThis area has carpet flooring, exposed wooden ceiling beams. Walk in wardrobe\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.65m (8'8\") x 2.8m (9'2\")\nThis area has carpet flooring. SE facing velux windows with lake view. Vaulted ceiling with exposed wooden beams\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.9m (12'10\") x 2.6m (8'6\")\nThis room has carpet flooring. Vaulted ceiling with exposed wooden beams. SW facing window with great views.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
